---
import AeoGuide from '../../layouts/AeoGuide.astro';
import { WW_STATE_NAMES, WW_STATE_COUNT_WORD } from '../../data/footprint';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'We used to sell a box or semi-custom line. Is Shiloh a replacement?', a: 'That is a common path. Shiloh is built-to-order face-frame and inset from WW Wood — plywood box, paint program, ~6-week lead — so you can step off a box line without standing up a full custom shop for every job.' },
  { q: 'We already build custom. Why add Shiloh?', a: 'Factory-backed Shiloh covers the jobs that should not eat the shop: modification range, Sherwin-Williams paint, six inset styles, furniture vanities. You keep true custom for the one-offs. Many Western dealers run both.' },
  { q: 'Do I need a consumer showroom to apply?', a: 'No. Pinnacle is a manufacturer’s rep. The dealer is the customer. Custom shops, design-build, and kitchen dealers all apply on the same form. We do not publish a dealer list.' },
  { q: 'What other lines can we add if we grow past Shiloh?', a: 'Eclipse (frameless, same factory), Aspect (value), Vistora (closets), Pronorm (German fitted, nationwide), US Stone (surfaces). Ask your rep about WW Wood programs not shown on this site.' },
];
---
<AeoGuide
  slug="become-a-shiloh-dealer"
  title="Become a Shiloh Cabinetry Dealer — From Custom or a Box Line | Pinnacle Sales"
  description="Become a Shiloh dealer through Pinnacle Sales. For custom shops and dealers leaving a box or semi-custom line. Shiloh-only applications welcome."
  heading="Become a Shiloh Dealer"
  lede="Custom shop, or leaving a box line? Open Shiloh."
  faqs={faqs}
>

<p>Apply on the <a href="/become-a-dealer/#apply">Become a Dealer</a> page. Check Shiloh. Tell us what you build now and what you used to sell. That is enough to start the call.</p>

<h2>Two shops we talk to every week</h2>
<p><strong>You used to sell a box or semi-custom line.</strong> Clients now want more modification, a better box, inset, a paint they cannot get off a restricted deck. Shiloh is the step-up line: WW Wood, Dudley, Missouri, all-plywood, dovetail drawers, ~6-week lead. You are not asking your crew to become a custom shop overnight.</p>
<p><strong>You already build custom.</strong> Factory Shiloh covers the jobs that should not consume the bench — paint, inset, furniture vanities, a predictable lead. You keep true custom for the one-offs. Shiloh is not a replacement for the shop. It is the line you sell when the shop should stay on the work that only you can build.</p>

<h2>Starting with Shiloh alone</h2>
<p>You can open <a href="/brands/shiloh-cabinetry/">Shiloh</a> alone. Face-frame and inset, six inset styles, Sherwin-Williams custom paint, White Oak and rift-cut without an upcharge. Eclipse is the same factory if you later want frameless — see <a href="/guides/face-frame-vs-frameless/">face-frame vs frameless</a>.</p>

<h2>Protected territory</h2>
<p>Shiloh is a WW Wood line. Pinnacle manages it across {WW_STATE_NAMES}. We don’t publish a dealer list; when homeowners ask us where to buy, we route them privately to an authorized dealer in their market. Apply, and we’ll tell you what is open. Map: <a href="/guides/protected-dealer-territories/">protected dealer territories</a>.</p>

<p><a href="/become-a-dealer/">Apply for Shiloh</a> — check the Shiloh box, note custom and any prior box line, submit.</p>

</AeoGuide>
